M4.18 commercial readiness implementation diagnosis
Date: 2026-08-28
Status: controlled local validation finding; no server action occurred

Finding M4_18_LOCAL_GATE_NOT_EXECUTABLE
- The first test run could not start the newly added read-only gate because the
  file mode was 0644 rather than executable.
- All ten tests failed at process creation with PermissionError. They did not
  execute contract logic, mutate a fixture or contact the server.

Cause
- The content was added through the repository patch workflow, which created a
  regular non-executable file. The test intentionally invokes the checked-in
  script directly to verify its operational file contract.

Approved bounded correction
- Set only scripts/tu1nz_adult_commercial_readiness_gate.py to mode 0755.
- Repeat compilation, the complete M4.18 test module and the exact local
  candidate gate before any Tailscale/SSH observation.

Rollback
- Before commit, abandon the M4.18 branch or remove its uncommitted artifacts.
- After commit, use a normal Git revert. No server rollback exists because this
  finding and correction are local repository metadata only.

Resolution M4_18_LOCAL_GATE_NOT_EXECUTABLE
- The gate mode is now 0755.
- Compilation, all ten then-expanded negative/positive tests, and the exact
  candidate gate completed successfully before SSH inventory.

Finding M4_18_CONTROL_BASELINE_STALE_LOCAL_CLONE
- The first local Control checkout was clean but 24 commits behind its remote.
- The M4.18 branch was created from freshly fetched origin/control-main at
  0467b6354f0202b95c86c17bdca6c45dfd1626d5, not from the stale local branch.
- No reset or rewrite was applied to the user's original local control-main
  branch.

Finding M4_18_CANONICAL_CONTROL_AUTORESET
- On the server, tu1nz_agentmode.service invokes tu1nz_sync_all.sh every five
  minutes.
- The script performs git fetch followed by git reset --hard @{u} in
  /opt/tu1nz_repos/control.
- The checkout was clean and exactly at 0467b6354f0202b95c86c17bdca6c45dfd1626d5,
  but it is an automatically mutated worktree and is prohibited as a staging
  target. Future Control releases must be clean immutable SHA-named clones.

Finding M4_18_APPLICATION_REVIEW_CHAIN_UNMERGED
- Candidate 183c5479246a27e7844670bf53c7e34200de92ea is an open, mergeable Draft
  PR #58 with four green checks.
- It is stacked on Draft PRs #49 through #57 and is not main-reachable.
- Activation remains NO-GO until the chain is merged in order and the final
  main-reachable application SHA is rebound in release evidence.

Finding M4_18_BACKUP_NOT_CANDIDATE_BOUND
- The current encrypted archive
  tu1nz_system_backup_20260828T03-31-58Z.tar.gz is present locally and remotely,
  is 45142464 bytes and has SHA-256
  5110d1e85d4256e22af6ad44cf23cb0333cd759c763219ce35a10dcc0f1496e5.
- The daily restore smoke test passed for that exact archive at
  2026-08-28T06:16:52Z.
- The archive contains existing Control/application/S1 material but no member
  named for M4.17 SHA 183c5479246a27e7844670bf53c7e34200de92ea.
- It is valid current-host evidence and not an activation backup for M4.17.

Finding M4_18_RCLONE_CONFIG_SAVE_WARNING
- The successful backup journal includes a nonfatal rclone error when it tried
  to create a temporary updated config on a read-only filesystem.
- Transfer completed 1/1, the service returned success, the exact remote object
  exists and the later restore-smoke test passed.
- A later activation backup must explicitly resolve or re-prove this behavior;
  M4.18 changes no rclone configuration.

Finding M4_18_VPN_MAINTENANCE_RISK
- Three Tailscale pings reached the exact host only through DERP(nue); no direct
  connection was established.
- The Mac CLI reports version 1.86.2 while its local daemon reports 1.86.4.
- SSH was stable for both chatops and root read-only checks. No VPN update or
  ACL change was performed.

Final diagnosis decision
- New commercial paths, identities, service, cron references, Docker mounts,
  processes and privileged open-file references are absent.
- PostgreSQL 17.11 listens only on 127.0.0.1:5432 and its local socket.
- M4.18 is GO for documentation, Control contract and preflight completion.
- Installation, activation, migration, exact-release backup/restore, provider
  access, real media/payment and production remain NO-GO.

Finding M4_18_UNITTEST_DISCOVERY_FALSE_ZERO
- A generic `python3 -m unittest discover -v` invocation returned success after
  running zero tests because this repository's test directory is exercised as
  explicit namespace modules rather than a discovery package.
- That zero-test result is rejected as evidence.
- The bounded correction is to run all four named Control test modules exactly
  as the workflow does; no package marker or production behavior is changed.

Resolution M4_18_UNITTEST_DISCOVERY_FALSE_ZERO
- The four explicit modules ran 69 tests and all 69 passed.
- The M4.18 subset ran 12 positive/negative tests.
- The exact local application candidate gate also passed.

Finding M4_18_PR_CREATE_LOCAL_QUOTING
- The first local orchestration attempt to construct the Draft PR command was
  rejected before command execution because Markdown delimiter characters
  conflicted with the outer command string.
- No GitHub PR or other external change was created by that attempt.
- The bounded correction is a plain-text PR body without those delimiters,
  followed by an explicit PR-state check. No history rewrite is used.

Finding M4_18_LOCAL_REMOTE_TRACKING_REF_ABSENT
- The final local `rev-parse` of the feature remote-tracking name failed even
  though the push and Draft PR succeeded.
- The clone intentionally fetches only
  `refs/heads/control-main:refs/remotes/origin/control-main`; the branch's
  upstream configuration exists, but this narrow refspec does not materialize
  feature remote-tracking refs locally.
- A direct read-only `git ls-remote` and GitHub PR query both returned
  b01c8ba9c568e30fe12fb1cb11c6f9e5d57b9a1f, exactly matching local HEAD.
- No user Git configuration or fetch refspec was changed.
